<section class="section section--hero">
  <div class="content stack">
    <span class="eyebrow">Our story</span>
    <h1 class="display">The oldest <em>call to prayer</em>.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Before clocks, before phones, the church bell kept the day and called the faithful in. Across America the towers have gone quiet. We exist to make them ring again.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--page">
  <div class="wrap grid grid--story">
    <div class="stack prose">
      <p class="m0">For centuries the church bell has been the Christian call to prayer — a swinging bell gathering the town for Sunday worship, the Angelus tolled at morning, noon and evening, peals for weddings and a slow toll in remembrance. A ringing bell tells a town, every day, that the church is alive and open.</p>
      <p class="m0">This is a serious undertaking, not a pastime. The Ding Dong Foundation, Inc. was certified by the IRS on July 28, 2026 as a 501(c)(3) public charity — approved fourteen days after filing. It pays for the work of ringing: bells and their towers, pipe organs, rose windows and stained glass, and the training of the artisans who keep them.</p>
      <p class="m0">There is more in a bell than announcement. Cast bronze rings at frequencies people have long found healing — a sound that settles a street, a room, a heart. Our filed purpose includes grants to those who work with sound, color and frequency for healing, and we honor it.</p>
    </div>
